# cyrius dep sidecar - stdlib leaves this fold requires in scope.
# Auto-generated by `cyrius distlib`; consumed by `cyrius deps`.
#
# ⛔⛔ AFTER EVERY `cyrius distlib`, DELETE THE `kashi_font_data` LINE IT RE-ADDS.
# kashi is VENDORED (`lib/kashi_font_data.cyr`, via `[deps.kashi] modules = ["src/font_data.cyr"]`) —
# it is neither a stdlib leaf nor something a consumer fetches through this sidecar. Listing it here
# makes `cyrius deps` in every consumer look for it in the stdlib and fail:
#     error: dep dhancha requires 'kashi_font_data' but it is not in the cyrius stdlib
# ⇒ A consumer supplies it by declaring `[deps.kashi]` itself, exactly as crab and puka do.
# ⚠ Cost of not knowing this: it blocked crab and puka from building against dhancha at all, and the
# first three diagnoses were wrong — a toolchain regression, then my own `lib sync --full` pollution,
# then dep ordering. It is none of those. Check this file FIRST when a consumer cannot resolve dhancha.
string
fmt
alloc
vec
str
io
args
syscalls
assert
bench
hashmap
fnptr
tagged
result
net
